        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: persistence prior on latest first-print/revised DOL CCSA level = 1.814 million; historical sample = 52 successive weekly changes in the DOL SA insured-unemployment history from June 28, 2025 to June 27, 2026; adjustment components = +0.008 million for recent continued-claims momentum and +0.004 million judgmental allowance for slower outflows with no initial-claims spike, giving point = 1.814 + 0.008 + 0.004 = 1.826 million. Using successive changes, sum of squared changes = 22932 thousand^2, sum of changes = -138 thousand, n = 52, sigma = sqrt((22932 - 138^2/52)/51) = 21.0 thousand = 0.021 million. One-week 80% half-width is about 1.28*sigma = 0.027 million; for the two-report horizon I scale by sqrt(2), giving 0.038 million, so bounds are 1.826 - 0.038 = 1.788 and 1.826 + 0.038 = 1.864."
